              "text": "Establishes that $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -k\\sqrt{h}$ and uses $h=10, \\frac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -2\\pi$ to find $k = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\sqrt{10}}$, so $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}V}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -\\frac{2\\pi}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{h}$."
            },
